.next
.git
*.md
.env*
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Secrets / credentials — must never enter the build context (defence in
# depth for docker:S6470; the `COPY . .` in the dev/builder stages reads it).
# All `.env*` are excluded: the build's only public input is the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL Docker ARG, not a committed env file, and
# the prod stage copies build artifacts only (.next/standalone, .next/static,
# public) — never source or env files. Note this CANNOT guard against a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_*-prefixed value: Next.js inlines those into the shipped JS
# bundle at build time, so never put a secret behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret
